(7667662, 1250414, 163081, '<td valign="top">not an expert on this matter but most probably the Tabanus australicus<br/></td>', 'not an expert on this matter but most probably the Tabanus australicus', '2020-06-23 01:56:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7667664, 1250414, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeorgesBogaert:</b></div><hr/><i> not an expert on this matter but most probably the Tabanus australicus </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thankyou so much for looking .. but i dont think its a march fly because of the large gap between its eyes .. <br/>i''m pretty sure the march flies eyes are very close together .. think that''s a sign of meanness in humans .. lol .. maybe in flies too .. ;)<br/> <br/><i>edit to say</i> ... of course i''d googled it .. and the front of the face itself looks quite different from the march flies .. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-06-23 01:13:58.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by GeorgesBogaert: not an expert on this matter but most probably the Tabanus australicus   thankyou so much for looking .. but i dont think its a march fly because of the large gap between its eyes .. i''m pretty sure the march flies eyes are very close together .. think that''s a sign of meanness in humans .. lol .. maybe in flies too .. ;) edit to say ... of course i''d googled it .. and the front of the face itself looks quite different from the march flies .. :)', '2020-06-23 02:11:00.000000', '2020-06-23 02:13:58.000000', 0),
(7667670, 1250925, 114285, '<td valign="top">Is this you, or a younger brother??</td>', 'Is this you, or a younger brother??', '2020-06-23 06:23:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7667671, 1250904, 38032, '<td valign="top">excellent!</td>', 'excellent!', '2020-06-23 06:24:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7667675, 1250867, 60581, '<td valign="top">I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2020-06-23 08:28:51.</i></td>', 'I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :) Originally posted by Kroburg: I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow. ', '2020-06-23 09:28:31.000000', '2020-06-23 09:28:51.000000', 0),
(7667680, 1250615, 115664, '<td valign="top">I LOVE THIS!!!</td>', 'I LOVE THIS!!!', '2020-06-23 10:17:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7667739, 1250867, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pgirish007:</b></div><hr/><i> I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow. </i></td></tr></table> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hey Girish .. are you saying that the stars in the sky were added in the preset .. and weren''t from your photos ..  <br/>i was under the impression that anything we used in an extended edit ... and that had a big effect on the image .. would have to be from one of our own photos .. <br/>like all the bokeh effects i add in my extended edits are from photos i''ve taken with the intention of adding them to my photos .. <br/>very interested to hear about this one .. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by pgirish007: I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :) Originally posted by Kroburg: I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow.    hey Girish .. are you saying that the stars in the sky were added in the preset .. and weren''t from your photos ..  i was under the impression that anything we used in an extended edit ... and that had a big effect on the image .. would have to be from one of our own photos .. like all the bokeh effects i add in my extended edits are from photos i''ve taken with the intention of adding them to my photos .. very interested to hear about this one .. :)', '2020-06-23 18:26:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7667876, 1250898, 122678, '<td valign="top">Magnificent</td>', 'Magnificent', '2020-06-24 09:02:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7668066, 1250867, 60581, '<td valign="top">Let''s see if this helps, Stars were all there, here is the image, right one is what camera captured with some adjustments and left one with that studio preset that I mentioned. if you look at the right one, all stars are there including the depth of Milky way, what preset did was did some glow kind of thing around the stars to pop those star irrespective of the color or size.<br/> <br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1251324" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60581/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1251324.png'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60581/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1251324.png'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60581/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1251324.png"/></a> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pgirish007:</b></div><hr/><i> I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow. </i></td></tr></table> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hey Girish .. are you saying that the stars in the sky were added in the preset .. and weren''t from your photos ..  <br/>i was under the impression that anything we used in an extended edit ... and that had a big effect on the image .. would have to be from one of our own photos .. <br/>like all the bokeh effects i add in my extended edits are from photos i''ve taken with the intention of adding them to my photos .. <br/>very interested to hear about this one .. :) </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Let''s see if this helps, Stars were all there, here is the image, right one is what camera captured with some adjustments and left one with that studio preset that I mentioned. if you look at the right one, all stars are there including the depth of Milky way, what preset did was did some glow kind of thing around the stars to pop those star irrespective of the color or size.   Originally posted by roz: Originally posted by pgirish007: I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :) Originally posted by Kroburg: I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow.    hey Girish .. are you saying that the stars in the sky were added in the preset .. and weren''t from your photos ..  i was under the impression that anything we used in an extended edit ... and that had a big effect on the image .. would have to be from one of our own photos .. like all the bokeh effects i add in my extended edits are from photos i''ve taken with the intention of adding them to my photos .. very interested to hear about this one .. :) ', '2020-06-26 19:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7668068, 1250867, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pgirish007:</b></div><hr/><i> Let''s see if this helps, Stars were all there, here is the image, right one is what camera captured with some adjustments and left one with that studio preset that I mentioned. if you look at the right one, all stars are there including the depth of Milky way, what preset did was did some glow kind of thing around the stars to pop those star irrespective of the color or size.<br/> <br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1251324" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60581/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1251324.png'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60581/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1251324.png'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/60581/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1251324.png"/></a> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pgirish007:</b></div><hr/><i> I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow. </i></td></tr></table> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hey Girish .. are you saying that the stars in the sky were added in the preset .. and weren''t from your photos ..  <br/>i was under the impression that anything we used in an extended edit ... and that had a big effect on the image .. would have to be from one of our own photos .. <br/>like all the bokeh effects i add in my extended edits are from photos i''ve taken with the intention of adding them to my photos .. <br/>very interested to hear about this one .. :) </i></td></tr></table> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hey Girish .. thanks so much for showing me what you have done .. <br/>it all makes sense now .. congratulations again on such an awesome image .. love what you did to it .. you really made it pop .. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by pgirish007: Let''s see if this helps, Stars were all there, here is the image, right one is what camera captured with some adjustments and left one with that studio preset that I mentioned. if you look at the right one, all stars are there including the depth of Milky way, what preset did was did some glow kind of thing around the stars to pop those star irrespective of the color or size.   Originally posted by roz: Originally posted by pgirish007: I used Topaz Studio with "City flare" presets and that did all that to me. :) Originally posted by Kroburg: I would love to know how you did that sky. Really well done. The only reason I didn''t vote as high as most other voters (I gave you a 6) is the blending of sky and land, where a clear white transition is quite distracting. But overall a very nice image. Congrats on the Yellow.    hey Girish .. are you saying that the stars in the sky were added in the preset .. and weren''t from your photos ..  i was under the impression that anything we used in an extended edit ... and that had a big effect on the image .. would have to be from one of our own photos .. like all the bokeh effects i add in my extended edits are from photos i''ve taken with the intention of adding them to my photos .. very interested to hear about this one .. :)    hey Girish .. thanks so much for showing me what you have done .. it all makes sense now .. congratulations again on such an awesome image .. love what you did to it .. you really made it pop .. :)', '2020-06-26 19:49:00.000000', NULL, 0),
